%N A399022 Triangle T(n, k), n >= 0, k = 0..n, read by rows; the n-th row lists the earliest starting offsets of the n+1 distinct subwords of length n in the infinite Fibonacci word (A003849).
%C A399022 Every nonnegative integer appears in the sequence (as A003849 is not ultimately periodic).
%H A399022 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="/A399022/b399022.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10010</a>
%H A399022 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="/A399022/a399022.gp.txt">PARI program</a>
%F A399022 Empirically, T(n, n) + n = A344953(n) for n > 0.
%e A399022 Triangle T(n, k) begins:
%e A399022     0
%e A399022     0 1
